    "title": "pandas.Index.nbytes — pandas 2.3.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "pandas.Index.nbytes# property Index.nbytes[source]# Return the number of bytes in the underlying data. Examples For Series: >>> s = pd.Series(['Ant', 'Bear', 'Cow']) >>> s 0 Ant 1 Bear 2 Cow dtype: object >>> s.nbytes 24 For Index: >>> idx = pd.Index([1, 2, 3]) >>> idx Index([1, 2, 3], dtype='int64') >>> idx.nbytes 24",
